From 349af363de0ec9cd26938fd2a00ac82df6663dec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:21:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] feat(gateway): forward the audit API to the control
 plane

GET /api/v1/audit-events was only reachable on the control plane
itself: the gateway's proxy routes did not include it, so requests
through the documented entry point got 404.

The path joins proxyRoutes like the other resource routes (exact path
and subtree), so it goes through the same chain: the API key is
checked, the tenant header is overwritten with the verified tenant,
requests count against the tenant's rate limit, the correlation id is
passed through, and path and query reach the control plane unchanged.
As for the other resource routes, the gateway does not check scopes;
the control plane enforces the read scope with the forwarded
credentials.

The README adds the path to the prefixes the gateway forwards and drops
the note from the REST API table. The gateway README, the CHANGELOG
entry and the OpenAPI operation no longer say that the gateway returns
404 for this path.
